Changes from upstream (v2 spec §1.2, X-27): the duplicated example
(duplicate_prompt_examples) is removed. Kept verbatim: the --PR Info--
block with the title and today's date, the diff fenced with ====== under
"The PR Diff:", and the final line followed by an open ```yaml fence (DQ-7;
the YAML loader's sign-off handling depends on it). The pipeline's one
re-ask inserts its note on its own line before the final line. Jinja
whitespace control is reproduced with {{- and -}}.

Intentional deviation (v2 spec §1.2, "title, description, branches"):
upstream sends the title and the date only. The PR Info block also carries
"Branch: '<source>'", "Target branch: '<target>'" (omitted when the pull
request has none) and the description fenced with ====== under "PR
Description:" (omitted when empty), worded as in pr_review's and
pr_describe's prompts.

Intentional deviation (v2 spec §1.2, X-13): upstream's
suggestion_discussion_context block (prior code-suggestion threads as JSON
data, with its instruction paragraph after the data) is replaced by
pr_review's existing-discussion block (.discussion, already rendered: the
fixed header DiscussionHeader, the only instruction in it, and the human
threads inside an adaptive code fence). It sits where upstream's block
sits, after the diff; without one nothing is rendered.

Intentional deviation (v2 spec §1.2, X-22): when context.repo.enabled is set
and uses of the changed symbols were found outside the pull request, the
pipeline supplies pr_review's repository-context block (.repo_context:
repoctx.Header and the fenced entries). As in pr_review, it follows the PR
Info block and precedes the part line and the diff; without one nothing is
rendered.

Intentional deviation (X-32): upstream has no project guidelines and no
file tree. The pipeline supplies pr_review's two blocks when they are on and
not empty: .guidelines (projctx.GuidelinesHeader with the path, and the
guidelines file read at the pull request's base revision, fenced and cut at
a line boundary) and .file_tree (projctx.TreeHeader and the fenced listing
of the directories the change touches, at the base revision). They follow
the PR Info block, guidelines first, and precede the repository context, the
part line and the diff, as in pr_review's prompt (pr_improve has no CI
block, and its discussion block follows the diff); without them nothing is
rendered.

Intentional deviation (v2 spec §1.3, X-19): when the pull request is
improved in several parts, each part's prompt gets one line (.part_header,
the fixed sentence of PartHeader) right before the diff. With one part
nothing is rendered.
*/ -}}
